From dd78443c6d67e888151b8d24214b1c518869de28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:45:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: align typed Chronik host and worker diagnostics
 across providers

Convert the same five diagnostics in Rust and native hosts, preserving Info
level, complete short static messages, raw native TxIds, returns and worker
queue/barrier/shutdown behavior. Do not change indexing, transaction formats,
database schema, block-file pointers or credential handling. The new focused
fresh-node fixture queries the real enabled index tip before a clean stop and
checks the actual stopping event. Rare queue failure, stop exception and missing
spent-coin paths are not newly forced; arbitrary exception strings retain the
existing bounded Error/truncation-flag contract.

This is a separate post381 background group. Native/Rust compilation and
runtime validation are pending and must not delay current integration/benches.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py0.51.0; ten reviewed mirrored sites):
